; status: works — a paper edge is a segment bundle just like a named crease
; (ADR 0014): `--cd & .c` selects the boundary piece of the top edge
; incident to corner .c. `--v` here is a flat (unfolded) mark, so the two
; halves of --cd stay at their own distinct table positions — folding the
; .c-side segment onto --v moves .c to the fold's mirror point.
paper square
mark --v = map .a onto .b
fold map --cd & .c onto --v toward .a moving .c

; assert .c = (1/2, 1/2)
